to specific basic helix-loop-helix transcription factors.</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>3033</fpage><lpage>3044</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15486100</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000352-Leivar1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leivar</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Monte</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Sady</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Carle</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Storer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The Arabidopsis phytochrome-interacting factor PIF7, together with PIF3 and PIF4, regulates responses to prolonged red light by modulating phyB levels.</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18252845</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000352-Quail1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quail</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Phytochrome Interacting Factors.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Garry</surname><given-names>Whitelam</given-names></name><name><surname>Karen</surname><given-names>Halliday</given-names></name></person-group><comment><italic>Light and Plant Development</italic>, Ch. 4, Blackwell Publishing</comment><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>105</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000352-Monte1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Monte</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tepperman</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Sady</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kac